import{_ as o,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CIO_ahoo.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Error codes","description":"Every reason code the facilitator answers verify and settle with, what it means, and what to do about it.","frontmatter":{"description":"Every reason code the facilitator answers verify and settle with, what it means, and what to do about it."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"reference/error-codes.md","filePath":"reference/error-codes.md"}'),d={name:"reference/error-codes.md"};function r(i,e,c,s,l,h){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="error-codes" tabindex="-1">Error codes <a class="header-anchor" href="#error-codes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Error codes&quot;">​</a></h1><p>A refused verify answers <code>isValid: false</code> with the code in <code>invalidReason</code>; a failed settle answers <code>success: false</code> with it in <code>errorReason</code>. Both use one vocabulary: the codes the <a href="https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/blob/main/specs/schemes/exact/scheme_exact_canton.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Canton <code>exact</code> scheme</a> and <a href="https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/blob/main/specs/x402-specification-v2.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">x402 v2</a> define, plus one of this implementation&#39;s own, marked below. Match on the code.</p><p><code>extensions.detail</code>, when present, says which of a code&#39;s causes it was, where the code alone leaves two apart. <code>invalidMessage</code> and <code>errorMessage</code> are free text for logs and people: they change between releases, so never match on them.</p><h2 id="the-payment-does-not-match" tabindex="-1">The payment does not match <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-payment-does-not-match" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The payment does not match&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The signed transfer is not the payment you asked for. Nothing was submitted, and the same payload will be refused again: the payer has to build a new payment.</p><ul><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_amount_mismatch</code>: The transfer moves a different amount from <code>amount</code>. The amount must be equal, not merely enough.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_merchant_mismatch</code>: The transfer pays someone other than <code>payTo</code>.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_instrument_id_mismatch</code>: The transfer moves a different instrument from <code>extra.instrumentId</code>, or the facilitator does not settle that instrument (detail <code>unserved_instrument</code>).</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_memo_mismatch</code>: The transfer&#39;s <code>x402.memo</code> differs from <code>extra.memo</code>, or carries one you did not quote.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_expired</code>: The transfer&#39;s own deadline (<code>executeBefore</code>) is past, or under 5 seconds away.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_preapproval_missing</code>: The transfer would not land directly at <code>payTo</code>, which needs a live <code>TransferPreapproval</code>. Without one it becomes an offer the merchant must accept, which the facilitator refuses to relay.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_insufficient_inputs</code>: The holdings the transfer spends are missing, repeated, or do not cover the amount.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_synchronizer_mismatch</code>: <strong>This implementation&#39;s own.</strong> The transfer was prepared on a different synchronizer from <code>extra.synchronizerId</code>. The spec defines no code for it; another facilitator may answer <code>invalid_exact_canton_malformed_payload</code>.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_self_payment</code>: The payer is the facilitator&#39;s own party.</li></ul><h2 id="the-payment-is-not-well-formed" tabindex="-1">The payment is not well-formed <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-payment-is-not-well-formed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The payment is not well-formed&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_missing_proof</code>: The payload is missing <code>preparedTransaction</code>, <code>preparedTxHash</code> or <code>signature</code>.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_malformed_payload</code>: The proof does not decode, or is not one transfer through the instrument&#39;s real <code>TransferFactory</code>. The detail names the part: <code>undecodable</code> (it will not gunzip), <code>structure_undecodable</code> (it gunzips but cannot be read), <code>payload_shape</code>, <code>unsupported_hashing_scheme</code>, or a <code>factory_</code> detail.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_signature_invalid</code>: The signature does not prove the payer signed this transaction: <code>no_payer_key</code> (the party publishes no key the facilitator can use), <code>malformed_encoding</code> (the hash or signature is not in the spec&#39;s encoding), <code>hash_mismatch</code> (the hash describes a different transaction) or <code>bad_signature</code> (it verifies under none of the party&#39;s keys).</li></ul><h2 id="the-requirements-are-wrong" tabindex="-1">The requirements are wrong <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-requirements-are-wrong" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The requirements are wrong&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The merchant&#39;s side needs fixing, not the payer&#39;s.</p><ul><li><code>invalid_payload</code>: The body is not an x402 v2 request: <code>{ x402Version: 2, paymentPayload, paymentRequirements }</code>, with <code>paymentPayload.accepted</code> a whole set of requirements. Answered with HTTP <code>400</code>.</li><li><code>unsupported_scheme</code>: The scheme is not <code>exact</code>.</li><li><code>invalid_network</code>: The payment&#39;s network differs from the requirements&#39;, or is not the network this facilitator settles.</li><li><code>invalid_payment_requirements</code>: The requirements are malformed (for example an <code>instrumentId</code> without its <code>admin</code>, or an amount that is not atomic units), or a settle reuses an <code>extra.memo</code> this project has already settled under (detail <code>memo_already_used</code>).</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_fee_payer_mismatch</code>: <code>extra.feePayer</code> is not this facilitator&#39;s party. Take it from <a href="/canton-x402-sdk/pr-153/reference/http-api.html#get-v2-supported"><code>GET /v2/supported</code></a>.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_merchant_not_registered</code>: Your API key may not receive at <code>payTo</code> (detail <code>destination_not_allowed</code>): <code>payTo</code> must be a party your project owns.</li></ul><h2 id="settlement-outcomes" tabindex="-1">Settlement outcomes <a class="header-anchor" href="#settlement-outcomes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Settlement outcomes&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>settlement_pending</code>: <strong>Not a failure.</strong> The transaction was relayed and its outcome is not known yet. <code>transaction</code> names it. <strong>What to do:</strong> Do not ask for a new payment. Retrying the same payload is safe and answers <code>invalid_exact_canton_execute_failed</code> if the relay failed, but keeps answering <code>settlement_pending</code> even once it commits. A verify of a payment already relayed answers the same way, with the transaction in <code>extra</code>. See <a href="/canton-x402-sdk/pr-153/guides/pending-payments.html">Pending payments</a>.</li><li><code>invalid_exact_canton_execute_failed</code>: The ledger rejected the transaction. Also the answer to a replay of one that failed. <strong>What to do:</strong> The payer builds a new payment.</li></ul><h2 id="faults" tabindex="-1">Faults <a class="header-anchor" href="#faults" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Faults&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>unexpected_canton_ledger_error</code>: The facilitator could not read the ledger: the payer&#39;s keys (detail <code>payer_keys_unavailable</code>) or the ledger&#39;s position before submitting (<code>ledger_end_unavailable</code>). Nothing was submitted. <strong>What to do:</strong> Retry the same payload.</li><li><code>unexpected_verify_error</code>: A fault in the facilitator during verify. HTTP <code>500</code>. <strong>What to do:</strong> Retry.</li><li><code>unexpected_settle_error</code>: A fault during settle. HTTP <code>500</code>, or <code>503</code> with <code>Retry-After</code> and detail <code>capacity_exhausted</code> when the facilitator is out of ledger capacity for the day, in which case nothing was submitted. <strong>What to do:</strong> Retry the same payload, after <code>Retry-After</code> if given.</li></ul><h2 id="defined-but-not-answered" tabindex="-1">Defined but not answered <a class="header-anchor" href="#defined-but-not-answered" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Defined but not answered&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The specs also define <code>invalid_exact_canton_execute_before_too_far</code>, <code>insufficient_funds</code>, <code>invalid_scheme</code>, <code>invalid_transaction_state</code> and <code>invalid_x402_version</code>. The SDK accepts them in an answer, but this facilitator does not send them: a body whose <code>x402Version</code> is not <code>2</code> is <code>invalid_payload</code>, and a payer without the funds cannot sign a transfer to begin with.</p>',17)])])}const f=o(d,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,f as default};
